{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Site Log API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Sync, uploads, realtime and team API for the Site Log iOS and Android apps.\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Error contract: every error code and what the app does</b></summary>\n\nEvery error has one shape, never a stack trace: `{\"error\":{\"code\":\"invalid_key\",\"message\":\"Key has the wrong shape\"}}`\n\n| Status | Codes | The app | Sent for |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `400` | `invalid_body` `bad_request` `invalid_key` `invalid_parts` `size_mismatch` `invalid_email` `invalid_role` | Permanent: **abort the job** | Malformed body, bad key, wrong size, missing parts |\n| `401` | `missing_token` `invalid_token` `member_removed` | Refresh the token once, retry; `member_removed` → sign out | Missing, expired, revoked or malformed token (never `403`); member removed |\n| `403` | `forbidden` `not_invited` | Permanent: show \"not allowed\", do not retry | The role may not do this or the project is not reachable; signed in but not a member |\n| `404` | `route_not_found` `upload_not_found` `object_not_found` `code_not_found` `member_not_found` `project_not_found` `invite_not_found` | Permanent | Unknown or aborted upload, nothing uploaded, unknown code, member, project, invite or route |\n| `409` | `already_completed` `already_member` `invite_used` `invite_expired` `invite_accepted` `email_mismatch` `last_admin` | `already_completed` on `complete` = success (body carries the stored result); others: show the reason | Same key completed by another upload; invite already used, expired or accepted; last Admin |\n| `413` | `body_too_large` `file_too_large` | Permanent | Body over 1 MiB, file over the upload limit |\n| `429` | `rate_limited` | Transient: wait, then retry | Rate limit |\n| `500` | `internal` | Transient: retry with backoff | Server fault |\n| `503` | `auth_unavailable` | Transient: retry with backoff | Firebase cannot be reached to check the token |\n\n- `200` includes a repeated `complete` or `DELETE`: both are safe to retry.\n- A `403` from **S3** on a presigned URL (XML body) means the URL expired; a `403` from the **API** (JSON `error` body) means the role or project access says no.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>WebSocket `/ws`: realtime upload results</b></summary>\n\n- Connect to `wss://<host>/ws` (`ws://localhost:3000/ws` locally). Not in the route list: Swagger cannot describe a WebSocket.\n- One JSON object per text frame, at most 64 KiB.\n- The token goes in the first message only, never in the URL.\n\n#### Messages\n\n| Direction | Message | When |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| App → server | `{\"type\":\"auth\",\"token\":\"<Firebase ID token>\"}` | **First**, within 5 s |\n| App → server | `{\"type\":\"subscribe\",\"sessionID\":\"<uuid>\"}` | Watch one capture session |\n| App → server | `{\"type\":\"ping\",\"at\":1764000000000}` | Keep-alive; any number |\n| Server → app | `{\"type\":\"snapshot\",\"sessionID\":\"<uuid>\",\"completed\":[{\"jobID\":\"<uploadId>\",\"remoteKey\":\"<remoteKey>\",\"sha256\":\"<sha256>\",\"verified\":true}],\"failed\":[{\"jobID\":\"<uploadId>\",\"reason\":\"integrity\"}]}` | Always first after `subscribe`: the catch-up |\n| Server → app | `{\"type\":\"jobCompleted\",\"jobID\":\"<uploadId>\",\"remoteKey\":\"<remoteKey>\",\"sha256\":\"<sha256>\",\"verified\":false}` | After `complete`, and again with `verified: true` once the worker re-read the file |\n| Server → app | `{\"type\":\"jobFailed\",\"jobID\":\"<uploadId>\",\"reason\":\"integrity\"}` | `integrity` (stored bytes differ) or `aborted` |\n| Server → app | `{\"type\":\"pong\",\"at\":1764000000000}` | Same number as the ping |\n\n- `jobID` is the `uploadId` from `/uploads`.\n- Trust `jobCompleted` only if its `sha256` equals the local hash.\n- Delivery is at most once: the `snapshot` after every `subscribe` is how the app catches up after a reconnect.\n\n#### Close codes\n\n| Code | Meaning | The app |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `4000` | No `auth` within 5 s | Reconnect, send `auth` first |\n| `4001` | Token missing, invalid or expired, or a message sent before `auth` | Refresh the token, reconnect |\n| `4003` | Not a member, or subscribed to another account's session | Not a member: ask an Admin to invite you. Other session: bug, do not retry it |\n| `4008` | Too many sockets for this account | Close older sockets |\n| `1009` | Message over 64 KiB | Bug |\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><b>Flows: sync, uploads and integrity, step by step</b></summary>\n\n#### Sync: pull `/sync/pull`\n\n1. Send `{\"since\":0,\"limit\":500}`: `since` is the `nextRev` of the last pull, `0` for a full download.\n2. Apply `changes` per table. A row with `deletedAt` set is a tombstone: delete it locally.\n3. `hasMore: true` → pull again at once with `since = nextRev`.\n4. `resyncRequired: true` → the cursor is older than the tombstone purge, or your access changed: wipe synced data and pull from `0`.\n\nEvery row carries a company-wide `rev` (one counter, locked per push), so no change is ever skipped, whatever the device clocks say.\n\n#### Sync: push `/sync/push`\n\n1. Send up to 200 `mutations`, parents first. `upsert` sends the **full row** in `fields`; `delete` sends `{}`.\n2. The batch runs in one transaction; each mutation gets its own result.\n3. The last write wins by `clientUpdatedAt`; a delete wins a tie; a deleted row never comes back.\n\n| Result | Meaning | The app |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `applied` | Stored | Mark the mutation done |\n| `superseded` | The server holds a newer row, a tombstone, or a row with the same natural key | Replace the local row with `serverRow` (its `id` may differ) |\n| `rejected` | Can never be stored as sent: `reason` says why (`missing_parent`, `forbidden:<action>`, `invalid_row:<code>`…) | Drop the mutation, log `reason` |\n\n#### Upload a file\n\nThe API never sees the bytes: the app PUTs them straight to S3 on presigned URLs.\n\n1. `/uploads` with `key`, `byteSize`, `contentType`, `sha256`. Under 5 MiB → `single` (one URL); from 5 MiB → `multipart` (8 MiB parts, every part URL at once).\n2. PUT the bytes (or each part) to S3 with `Content-Type` equal to `contentType`. Keep each part's `ETag` header.\n3. A `403` from S3 = the URL expired: `/uploads/{id}/parts/refresh` for the parts still to send (multipart), or begin again (single).\n4. `/uploads/{id}/complete`: `{}` for single, every part's `etag` for multipart. The server checks the object in S3, records the hash and returns `remoteKey` and `verificationCode`.\n5. To give up: `DELETE` `/uploads/{id}`.\n\n- `complete` is idempotent: a retry after a lost response returns the same body.\n- `409 already_completed` → another upload of the same key won; its body carries the stored result: treat as success.\n- `404 object_not_found` → nothing reached S3; `400 size_mismatch` → the stored size differs from `byteSize`.\n\n#### Integrity: from registered to verified\n\n| Step | Who | What it proves |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `registered` | `complete` | This account registered this hash at this time |\n| `verified` | Worker re-reads the object and recomputes SHA-256 | The stored bytes hash to this value |\n| `mismatch` | Worker hash differs | `jobFailed(integrity)` to the app |\n\n`verified` turns `true` later: the app learns it from the WebSocket (`jobCompleted`) or by pulling.\n\n</details>"
  },
